One aspect of my independent work that I find particularly encouraging is its ability to engage people across different professional backgrounds. Although I write about subjects that can become technically and conceptually complex, I deliberately approach them in a way that makes the underlying ideas accessible without sacrificing depth. My professional network includes people working in AI governance, software and infrastructure engineering, aerospace and defense, research, education, health, banking, and community development, among other fields. This has reinforced my interest in communicating and developing systems across disciplinary boundaries rather than approaching complex human and technological challenges from a single professional perspective.
:::
